{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. I see you came in with right upper belly pain and a fever. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. I’ve had this stabbing pain in my right side for about five days. It comes and goes. I also threw up once—non-bloody, non-bilious—and had a low fever yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you’ve been feeling nauseous since then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:32:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, still a bit nauseous. I took Zofran earlier and it helped a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You were on ertapenem at home for a recent cholangitis episode, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:33:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I got my dose before coming in. I was told to come back if I had fever or more vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good call. We’ve reviewed your labs and ultrasound. Your liver enzymes are a bit higher than last time, and the ultrasound shows your liver still looks cirrhotic with a little ascites and a small stone in the gallbladder remnant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why I’m having pain again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. The stone and some sludge in the bile duct could be causing inflammation—cholangitis. We’re not seeing a blockage, but it’s still concerning given your history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning an MRCP tomorrow to get a better look. If we see sludge or a blockage, we may do an ERCP to clean it out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I’m also a bit lightheaded when I stand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2179-03-22 20:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave you two liters of fluids in the ER, so we’ll keep an eye on that. Your blood pressure is stable now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2179-03-23 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood cultures came back negative—no infection in the blood. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2179-03-23 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Does that mean it’s not cholangitis again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2179-03-23 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. Cholangitis can still be localized to the bile ducts. We’re still concerned, especially with your symptoms and liver enzyme changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2179-03-23 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. What’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2179-03-23 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re scheduled for an MRCP this morning. It will help us see if there’s sludge or narrowing in the ducts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2179-03-24 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I have the MRCP results. There’s sludge in the distal common bile duct and a small stone in the gallbladder remnant—similar to what we saw on ultrasound."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2179-03-24 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s likely causing the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2179-03-24 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We also see your liver cirrhosis and portal hypertension—varices, ascites, splenomegaly—all consistent with your known condition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2179-03-24 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another ERCP?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2179-03-24 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve scheduled one for tomorrow. We’ll use a balloon to sweep out the sludge. It’s a routine procedure for this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2179-03-24 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And antibiotics? I’m still on ertapenem."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2179-03-24 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching you to meropenem. Infectious disease recommends it due to your history of resistant infections. It’s stronger and given more frequently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2179-03-24 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe with my allergies?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2179-03-24 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’re allergic to penicillins and sulfa, but meropenem is a carbapenem—different class. We’ve checked, and it’s safe for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2179-03-25 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, great news. The ERCP went well. We found no strictures, and we removed some sludge from the bile duct with a balloon sweep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2179-03-25 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Did you see the stone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2179-03-25 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the small stone in the remnant gallbladder is still there, but it’s not blocking anything. We’ll monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2179-03-25 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the antibiotics—still meropenem?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2179-03-25 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, IV meropenem every eight hours. You’ll finish a seven-day course after the ERCP. We’ll arrange home health for the infusions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2179-03-25 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about my other meds? I usually take furosemide and spironolactone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2179-03-25 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We held them during this infection because you’re not retaining fluid right now. You can restart them after discharge unless you swell up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2179-03-25 13:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my PICC line—is it still good?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2179-03-25 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the chest X-ray shows it’s in a good position—tip in the right atrium. We’ll keep using it for antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs today look better—liver enzymes are coming down, white count is normal. You’ve been fever-free since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Does that mean I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discharging you today. You’ll continue meropenem at home for five more days via the PICC line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other medications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll restart furosemide and spironolactone. All your other meds—rifaximin, ursodiol, omeprazole, Synthroid—stay the same."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll need blood work—CBC, liver tests, kidney function—next week. We’ve given you a prescription. Please send the results to your liver doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the EGD and colonoscopy that were postponed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, reschedule those with your transplant clinic. The EGD last time showed no varices, which is good, but you’re due for a repeat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had an ulcer found on EGD—should I worry?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a small ulcer at the junction. Omeprazole should help it heal. Let your doctor know if you have black stools or severe pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my transplant status?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re still on the list. This episode hasn’t changed your status. Keep in close contact with the transplant team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. Home health will contact you about the IV antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I get a fever again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your liver doctor or go to the ER. Recurrent cholangitis is serious, but catching it early helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re glad we could help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—my headache is gone, and I haven’t felt nauseous since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. It means the treatment is working. Keep up with the fluids and rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in shortly with your discharge instructions and prescriptions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see you in follow-up. Feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good luck."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2179-03-26 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're all set."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2179-03-22 20:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2179-03-26 17:39:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with primary sclerosing cholangitis, cirrhosis, and a history of recurrent cholangitis was readmitted for recurrent right upper quadrant abdominal pain and low-grade fever. She had recently completed a course of ertapenem for a prior cholangitis episode. Imaging revealed biliary sludge and a small stone in the gallbladder remnant. An ERCP was performed, which showed no strictures and allowed for removal of sludge from the bile duct. Antibiotics were switched from ertapenem to meropenem for a targeted seven-day course post-procedure. Her symptoms resolved, liver enzymes improved, and she remained afebrile. She was discharged home with plans to continue IV meropenem via her existing PICC line, restart home diuretics, and follow up for lab monitoring and outpatient procedures. Her transplant status remains unchanged.",
    "problems": [
      "Cholangitis",
      "Awaiting organ transplant status",
      "Celiac disease",
      "Primary biliary cirrhosis",
      "Hepatic failure, unspecified without coma",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult) (pediatric)",
      "Pruritus, unspecified",
      "Personal history of nicotine dependence"
    ]
  }
}
